+# Bisect: land-the-textkit-batch
+
+## Change at fault
+
+`queue/002-search-case.patch` (search ignores case). Now `held` in QUEUE.md.
+
+Failure: `tests/search.test.mjs:19` "an exact title match comes first, the rest
+keep their order" — expected `[3, 2]`, actual `[3, 2, 4]`. The patch makes the
+search return an extra item (id 4) that the test expects to be excluded.
+
+## How it was found
+
+The full batch (001, 002, 003) failed that one test with 9 of 10 passing
+(`.grooph/land-the-textkit-batch/runs/20260922-051355/integrate-round0.txt`).
+Each change was then run through `npm run integrate` on its own by toggling
+statuses in QUEUE.md, and the remainder was re-run together:
+
+| run | queued | result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 001 alone | 001 | 8 pass, 0 fail |
+| 002 alone | 002 | 8 pass, 1 fail: search.test.mjs:19, actual `[3, 2, 4]` (same as the full batch) |
+| 003 alone | 003 | 8 pass, 0 fail |
+| batch minus 002 | 001, 003 | 9 pass, 0 fail |
+
+002 reproduces the failure by itself, and the batch without it is green, so 002
+is the change at fault and not an interaction between changes.
+
+## What stays queued
+
+In the original order:
+
+1. `queue/001-slug-accents.patch` — queued
+2. `queue/003-limit-negative.patch` — queued
+
+Nothing under `queue/`, `src/` or `tests/` was changed; no fix was attempted.
