+# Changes
+
+## This round
+
+- `src/format.mjs`: `formatMoney` computed its output using `Math.abs(cents)` but
+  never reapplied the sign, so negative amounts lost their `-` (e.g. `-123456`
+  rendered as `$1,234.56` instead of `-$1,234.56`). Added a `sign` variable
+  (`"-"` when `cents < 0`, else `""`) and prefixed the returned string with it,
+  before the currency symbol, so the sign appears in front of the symbol as
+  required.
+- No test changes were needed: `tests/format.test.mjs` already contained the
+  "a negative amount keeps its sign in front of the symbol" test covering this
+  behaviour; it now passes along with the rest of the suite (`npm test`: 7/7
+  passing).
+- Nothing under `queue/` or `QUEUE.md` was touched.
